hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15748","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Mu'awiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What about things we used to do in the Jahiliyyah, we used to take omens? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is something you find in yourself, so let it not turn you away. He said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to come to soothsayers. He said: Do not come to soothsayers."
